TI  - Periodontal Disease-Like Manifestations in Patients Having Acute Leukemia With 
      Normal Complete Blood Counts.
PG  - 6081296
LID - 10.1155/crid/6081296 [doi]
LID - 6081296
AB  - Acute leukemia (AL) is a malignant hematopoietic disease with a high fatality 
      rate, and early detection and diagnosis are crucial for subsequent treatment. 
      Clinically, oral manifestations, particularly the ones similar to those of 
      periodontal disease, may be the first signs of AL. The present study reports two 
      patients with complaints of gingival swelling and loosening of teeth, who had 
      normal routine blood clinical tests. After bone marrow puncture, the patients 
      were diagnosed with AL. Despite the blood tests being normal, abnormal gingival 
      manifestations and unexplained looseness of teeth should be treated with 
      suspicion, and AL should be considered a possible differential diagnosis.
