UOF - Res Sq. 2025 Oct 31:rs.3.rs-6933141. doi: 10.21203/rs.3.rs-6933141/v1. PMID: 
      41282106
PMC - PMC13216603
OAB - Computational models can be used to analyse images of cells and tissues taken 
      from people with cancer. Most models are designed for images of solid tissue and 
      do not base their analysis on the appearance of individual cells. This means they 
      do not work so well on liquid samples such as blood samples. We developed a 
      system to detect blood cancers from images of blood and found it worked better 
      than models previously developed for solid tissue analysis. Our computational 
      model could also be used by other researchers to discover additional diseases 
      detectable from blood samples or be expanded to enable population-scale blood 
      cancer screening.
