TI  - Unilateral Proptosis: A Rare Presenting Sign of Acute Myeloid Leukemia.
PG  - e400
LID - 10.5001/omj.2022.10 [doi]
AB  - Unilateral proptosis is a rare initial presenting sign of acute myeloid leukemia 
      (AML). We report a case of unilateral proptosis in a six-year-old girl as the 
      initial manifestation of AML. The cancer link was initially missed and the case 
      was investigated as one of hyperthyroidism. Peripheral blood smear and bone 
      marrow aspirate evaluation showed signs diagnostic of AML. Computed tomography 
      scan of orbits showed infiltrative process in the right orbit, right maxillary, 
      and right ethmoidal sinuses. Unilateral proptosis as an extramedullary first 
      presenting feature of AML is very rare; however, it should always be considered 
      in the differential diagnosis of proptosis in pediatric age group.
