IP  - 4
DP  - 2021
TI  - Acute Myeloid Leukemia with Myelodysplasia-Related Changes Presenting as Vitamin 
      B12 Deficiency: A Cautionary Tale.
PG  - 218-223
AB  - Acute myeloid leukemia may present with significant dysmyelopoiesis within the 
      peripheral blood smear and bone marrow aspirate. In the setting of Vitamin B12 
      deficiency, proliferation of a clonal population of malignant cells can become 
      impaired, masking an underlying myelodysplastic or leukemic process. Typically, 
      the cautionary tale warns against diagnosing acute myeloid leukemia before ruling 
      out Vitamin B12 deficiency. Here we describe a patient who initially presented 
      with pancytopenia and Vitamin B12 deficiency who, upon supplementation, developed 
      overt acute myeloid leukemia. This case will highlight the importance of 
      cytogenetic and molecular studies as essential diagnostic tools in patients with 
      unique presentations.
