AB  - A 75-year-old man was referred to our department because of discolouration of his 
      tongue and an elevated CRP. Clinical examination did not reveal any other 
      abnormalities. Blood examination showed an excessive amount of leukocytes with 
      low platelet and erythrocyte counts. These findings indicated an atypical 
      presentation of acute myeloid leukaemia.
