DP  - 2017 Jan
TI  - Case 237: Renal Cell Carcinoma with Osseous Metaplasia.
PG  - 293-298
LID - 10.1148/radiol.2016140817 [doi]
AB  - History A 47-year-old man presented with palpitations and decreased exercise 
      tolerance. A peripheral blood smear revealed anemia, thrombocytopenia, and blast 
      cells, and a diagnosis of acute myeloid leukemia was made. Immunohistochemistry 
      revealed positivity for cluster of differentiation (or CD) markers, which have 
      been reported to be associated with an increased risk of extramedullary leukemic 
      involvement. Thus, contrast material-enhanced computed tomography (CT) of the 
      thorax, abdomen, and pelvis was requested to enable exclusion of any 
      extramedullary extension of leukemia. Unenhanced and contrast-enhanced 
      nephrographic phase CT was performed. Follow-up CT 3 months later showed minimal 
      interval change in the lesion (images not shown).
