DP  - 2017 Mar
TI  - An unusual initial manifestation of acute myeloid leukemia.
PG  - 418-420
LID - 10.1177/0956462416671838 [doi]
AB  - Leukemia cutis is seen in around 20% of acute monocytic leukemia. They usually 
      present as papules or nodules or infiltrated plaques but ulceration is uncommon. 
      A 28-year-old female presented with multiple painless indurated genital ulcers of 
      three weeks' duration with low-grade fever, gum hyperplasia, and generalized 
      lymphadenopathy. Tissue smear from the edge of the ulcer showed atypical 
      monocytes suggestive of leukemic infiltrate which was further confirmed by 
      peripheral smear and bone marrow aspirate. Herein, we report a case of acute 
      monocytic leukemia (AML) with leukemia cutis presenting initially with genital 
      ulcers simulating chancre.
