TI  - Ptosis Shmosis.
PG  - 237-240
LID - S0039-6257(16)30012-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.survophthal.2016.02.004 [doi]
AB  - A 10-year-old girl presented with painless unilateral left upper lid ptosis. A 
      nontender hard mass was palpated in the left upper lid. Blood smear was 
      compatible with the diagnosis of leukemia. The cause of ptosis was now thought to 
      be a mass composed of myeloid blast cells (myeloid sarcoma).
