AB  - We present the case of a patient who presented cells with different morphologic 
      appearance, lymphoblasts on peripheral blood smear, lymphoblasts on bone marrow 
      aspirate and myloblasts on bone marrow biopsy, and immunophenotyping, leading to 
      different stage diagnosis. The final diagnosis was that of acute myeloid leukemia 
      (LAM0).
