TI  - Cup-like blasts in acute myeloid leukemia.
PG  - 847-8
LID - 10.1002/ajh.23954 [doi]
AB  - A patient with AML with normal karyotype and the cytological pattern of cup-like 
      blasts (CLB) is reported. The typical morphology on Pappenheim stained blood 
      smears is shown. In addition transmission electron microscopy pictures 
      demonstrate impressively the invaginated nuclear pocket compressing the 
      chromatin. Cup-like blasts usually do not express CD34. There is a close 
      relationship of CLB-AML with the molecular aberrations of NPM1 and/or FLT3-ITD.
