TI  - CNS Involvement in AML Patient Treated with 5-Azacytidine.
PG  - 937203
LID - 10.1155/2014/937203 [doi]
LID - 937203
AB  - Central nervous system (CNS) involvement in acute myeloid leukemia (AML) is a 
      rare complication of the disease and is associated with poor prognosis. Sometimes 
      the clinical presentation can be unspecific and the diagnosis can be very 
      challenging. Here we report a case of CNS infiltration in a patient suffering 
      from AML who presented with normal complete blood count and altered mental 
      status.
