TI  - [Investigation and management of patients presenting with thrombocytosis].
PG  - 465-71
LID - S0248-8663(13)00066-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.revmed.2013.02.020 [doi]
AB  - Thrombocytosis is a common finding when performing a blood count. It is often 
      consecutive to an underlying condition and then does not lead to thrombotic 
      complications. If a reactive thrombocytosis is eliminated, thrombocytosis is 
      primitive, rarely hereditary and most often associated with hematological 
      malignancies. Essential thrombocythemia must be recognized, by eliminating the 
      differential diagnoses that are myelodysplastic syndromes associated with 
      thrombocytosis and other myeloproliferative disorders. The treatment is based on 
      the prevention of thrombotic risk and the possible introduction of a 
      cytoreductive therapy. Life expectancy is close to that of the general population 
      and mainly depends on the occurrence of myelofibrosis or transformation to acute 
      myeloid leukemia.
