AB  - A morphology session is held each year at the Annual Scientific Meeting of the 
      British Society of Haematology. Prior to the meeting this year, eight morphology 
      cases were made available to BSH members as glass slides and also digitally as 
      'virtual slides'. A panel of invited commentators who had no prior knowledge of 
      the diagnosis discussed the eight cases. An initial limited history and blood 
      count are given with representative images from the case material; this is 
      followed by the discussants' comments and suggested diagnosis. The actual 
      clinical diagnosis is then given with other relevant information.
