TI  - Update on the therapy for myelodysplastic syndrome.
PG  - 177-86
LID - 10.1002/ajh.21352 [doi]
AB  - The myelodysplastic syndromes (MDS) are a diverse group of clonal hematopoietic 
      stem cell disorders characterized by cytopenias. Patients have a risk of 
      developing acute leukemia though most succumb to complications of low blood 
      counts. Over the past decade many novel treatments have been developed and 
      investigation of new agents is ongoing. In this article, we discuss the 
      classification and prognostic systems that are used in MDS, the agents available 
      for treatment of MDS as well as review supportive and palliative care options for 
      patients who are not candidates for, or opt against, newer treatment strategies.
