TI  - Adalimumab-induced acute myelogenic leukemia.
PG  - 1261-2
LID - 10.1097/SMJ.0b013e318188950a [doi]
AB  - Newer biological treatment strategies have been developed in the last decade with 
      some promising outcomes. Their safety, however, has been questioned lately with 
      multiple reports of increased risk for malignancies and infectious complications. 
      These reports render their use suboptimal. We report a 44-year-old woman 
      receiving adalimumab (Humira) for advanced juvenile rheumatoid arthritis who then 
      developed acute myelogenic leukemia.
