TI  - Acute lymphoblastic leukemia associated with brucellosis in two patients with 
      fever and pancytopenia.
PG  - 741-4
AB  - Brucellosis is a disease involving the lymphoproliferative system, which may lead 
      to changes in the hematological parameters; however, pancytopenia is a rare 
      finding. However, malignant diseases in association with brucellosis are rarely 
      the cause of pancytopenia. Herein, two cases with fever and pancytopenia, 
      diagnosed as simultaneous acute lymphoblastic leukemia and brucellosis are 
      presented. Anti-leukemic therapy and brucellosis treatment were administered 
      simultaneously, and normal blood parameters obtained. The first patient is in 
      complete remission; the other recovered from the brucellosis, but later died due 
      to a leukemic relapse.
