TI  - [Myeloproliferative disorders].
PG  - 131-42
AB  - Myeloproliferative disorders are caused by abnormalities of hematopoietic stem 
      cells leading to uncontrolled proliferation of one or more cell lines in the 
      blood. Besides sharing common clinical and hematologic features they are 
      characterized by clonal hematopoiesis and genetic instability, resulting in a 
      disease-specific rate of transformation into acute leukemia. This review 
      discusses relevant clinical and prognostic aspects as well as current diagnostic 
      and therapeutic procedures of polycythemia vera, essential thrombocythemia and 
      chronic idiopathic myelofibrosis.
