DP  - 2002 Jul
TI  - Cholecystitis as the presenting manifestation of acute myeloid leukemia: report 
      of a case.
PG  - 254-6
AB  - We report a case of acute leukemia, which presented as cholecystitis in a 
      previously healthy middle-aged adult. Leukemic involvement of the 
      gastrointestinal tract is a well-known clinicopathological entity. However, 
      leukemic infiltration of the gall bladder wall is a rare occurrence. It has only 
      been previously described in the setting of relapsed disease and, to our 
      knowledge, has never been reported as the primary manifestation of de novo acute 
      leukemia. The patient in question was treated with standard induction and 
      consolidation chemotherapy and remains in complete remission 19 months after his 
      presentation with symptoms consistent with cholecystitis.
