AB  - A 14-year-old girl presented with the acute onset of gastrointestinal symptoms 
      due to hypercalcaemia. Chest X-ray revealed osteolytic lesions in the ribs which 
      in conjunction with a normal parathyroid hormone level raised the possibility of 
