DP  - 2001 Sep-Oct
TI  - Multiple granulocytic sarcomas in acute myeloblastic leukemia with simultaneous 
      occurrence of t(8:21) and trisomy 8.
PG  - 1139-44
AB  - This report describes a rare case of multiple intracranial, extradural chloromas. 
      A five year old African American male presented with headache, fever, and 
      vomiting. The peripheral blood smear showed myeloblasts with Auer rods. The 
      CTscan of the brain showed three intracranial, epidural lesions as well as soft 
      tissue masses in the retroorbital region and sphenoid sinuses. CTscan of the 
      chest showed two paraspinal epidural thoracic masses. Pathology of the epidural 
      intracranial mass revealed a granulocytic sarcoma. Cytogenetic analysis showed 
      simultaneous occurrence of t(8;21) and trisomy 8. Following induction therapy, he 
      is now in complete remission.
