TI  - MRI of perineural extramedullary granulocytic sarcoma.
PG  - 492-5
AB  - Granulocytic sarcoma is an extramedullary solid tumour consisting of myelogenous 
      leukaemic blast cells, usually seen in acute myeloid leukaemia and less commonly 
      in patients with chronic myeloid leukaemia or myeloproliferative disorders. Blast 
      cells have a predilection for periosteal and perineural regions and rarely 
      precede evidence of systemic disease. We present two patients, aleukaemic on 
      peripheral blood counts, both at presentation and during subsequent treatment. We 
      present the MRI features of this rare but important condition.
