TI  - Orbital granulocytic sarcoma in acute myelogenous leukemia.
PG  - 234-5
AB  - A five year old boy presented with progressively increasing proptosis of the left 
      eye. CT scan showed bilateral extra-conal homogeneously enhancing soft tissue 
      masses, larger on the left side. A possibility of granulocytic sarcoma of the 
      orbit was considered. Diagnosis was confirmed by peripheral smear and bone marrow 
      aspiration. Patient responded to chemotherapy.
