TI  - Arthritic presentation of childhood leukaemia.
PG  - 562-4
AB  - Three cases of childhood acute lymphatic leukaemia masquerading as juvenile 
      chronic arthritis are presented. All had symptoms and signs for at least 4 months 
      before leukaemia was diagnosed and in two the full blood count was normal at 
      presentation. The importance of a high index of suspicion is emphasized, 
      particularly if the white cell count is low.
