DP  - 1989
TI  - Neuroimmunitary profile estimation in cerebrospinal fluid and its importance in 
      childhood acute lymphoblastic leukaemia.
PG  - 199-204
AB  - Immunoglobulin G (IgG) and albumin (Alb.) were measured in the cerebrospinal 
      fluid (CSF) of 14 children with acute lymphoblastic leukaemia (ALL), with and 
      without leukaemic infiltration of the central nervous system (CNS). The following 
      indexes: (formula; see text) were calculated and used to express a protein 
      profile of the CSF. This profile was found to be inflammatory-like in 10 children 
      (71%) and normal in 4 (29%). The first two indexes, that reflect a local 
      synthesis of IgG correlated significantly (r = 0.823; p less than 0.001). The 
      follow-up made in five children showed a relationship between clinical course and 
      local IgG synthesis.
