IS  - 0256-9574 (Print)
VI  - 73
IP  - 8
DP  - 1988 Apr 16
TI  - B-cell prolymphocytic leukaemia--clinical and haematological features.
PG  - 470-2
AB  - Prolymphocytic leukaemia is an unusual but distinctive variant of chronic 
      lymphocytic leukaemia which generally responds poorly to chemotherapy. Four cases 
      are described to illustrate typical clinical and haematological features and to 
      emphasise the unsatisfactory outcome with combination chemotherapy, radiotherapy 
      and plasma exchange in 3 patients, and to draw attention to the prolonged disease 
      control which followed splenectomy in the fourth. These observations illustrate 
      the relative ease with which the diagnosis can be made and also the difficulties 
      in management, which requires exploration of alternative treatment options.
