VI  - 29
IP  - 2
DP  - 1988 Feb
TI  - Spinal cord involvement as the presenting symptom of acute monocytic leukemia.
PG  - 145-8
AB  - Spinal cord involvement in leukemia is rare and has been described only once in 
      association with acute monocytic leukemia. A patient whose presenting symptom of 
      acute monocytic leukemia was the syndrome of cauda equina compression due to an 
      epidural and retroperitoneal leukemic mass is reported. Peripheral blood smears 
      were normal throughout the evolution of the disease. The radiological, surgical, 
      and pathological findings are presented, and the therapeutic, along with the 
      prognostic implications of spinal cord involvement by leukemia are discussed.
