DP  - 1986 Sep
TI  - Absolute neutrophilia in adult T cell leukemia.
PG  - 858-61
AB  - The numbers of neutrophils and platelets and the serum calcium (Ca) levels were 
      examined in 12 patients with lymphoma-type adult T cell leukemia (ATL) and 35 
      patients with leukemic-type ATL. The same parameters were also studied in 17 
      patients with non-Hodgkin's lymphoma and 22 patients with acute lymphocytic 
      leukemia as controls. The numbers of neutrophils and the serum Ca levels were 
      significantly higher in leukemic-type ATL (P less than 0.01) and lymphoma-type 
      ATL (P less than 0.05) than in the controls. However, no statistically 
      significant correlation between the numbers of neutrophils and the levels of 
      serum Ca in ATL was observed. Thus, these two abnormal clinical features might be 
      caused by different humoral factors.
