DP  - 1985
TI  - Treatment of dysmyelopoietic/leukemic syndromes with myelofibrosis and 
      megakaryocytic hyperplasia with large doses of cytosine arabinoside.
PG  - 87-91
AB  - Eight patients with inaspiratable bone marrows due to significant degrees of 
      fibrosis were treated with high dose cytosine arabinoside because of either 
      documented or suspected coexistent acute leukemia. The peripheral blood counts 
      returned to normal in 7 patients. Remissions were short lived and bone marrow 
      abnormalities persisted suggesting that consolidation therapy should be 
      administered to these patients as soon as their peripheral blood counts are 
      normalized.
