DP  - 1984 Sep
TI  - Transient erythroblastopenia of childhood. A review of 22 cases.
PG  - 266-70
AB  - In the period 1975-1983 22 patients, aged 4-36 months were seen with severe 
      transient normochromic, normocytic anaemia caused by a transient 
      erythroblastopenia. In 20 patients bone marrow aspirations were obtained; they 
      showed erythroblastopenia. In ten cases we observed young lymphoid cells, 
      suggesting a diagnosis of acute lymphoblastic leukaemia. One patient suspected of 
      a leukaemia, was studied in more detail. All patients showed reticulocytopenia. 
      MCV and HbF were within normal range. During recovery reticulocytosis and higher 
      levels of HbF were found. Except for blood transfusion in most patients, therapy 
      (e.g. corticosteroids) was not necessary. Spontaneous recovery is a feature of 
      this kind of erythroblastopenia, contrasting with congenital hypoplastic anaemia.
