      the myeloid and lymphocytic leukemias, with emphasis on findings in the blood 
      smear. Cell counts and their diagnostic significance are discussed. Data reported 
      are derived from a study of patients seen at the University of Rochester Medical 
      Center between 1970 and 1982.
