LR  - 20190825
IS  - 0145-2126 (Print)
IS  - 0145-2126 (Linking)
VI  - 7
IP  - 1
DP  - 1983
TI  - Glucocorticoid receptors in childhood acute non-lymphocytic leukemia.
PG  - 11-6
AB  - Using a whole-cell assay, we found glucocorticoid receptors (GR) in all 43 
      consecutive assessable children with newly diagnosed acute non-lymphocytic 
      leukemia (ANLL). The receptor levels ranged from 2146 to 81,308 sites/cell 
      (median = 18,105); these results were similar to those for acute lymphocytic 
      leukemia. Receptor levels were not related to any of these clinical or biological 
      features at diagnosis: age, sex, race, initial leukocyte count, liver or spleen 
      size, presence of CNS disease or Auer rods, [3H] thymidine ( [3H]TdR) labelling 
      index, French-American-British morphology or terminal deoxynucleotidyl 
      transferase activity. Receptor levels also were not related to the initial 
      treatment response or remission duration after therapy that did not include a 
      glucocorticoid. We conclude that GR level has no clinical utility as a marker 
      protein in childhood ANLL.
