TI  - Major bone lesions in acute lymphoblastic leukaemia.
PG  - 67-70
AB  - The records of 1471 patients with ALL entered into UKALL trials II-V (1972-1977) 
      were studied, and major bone lesions at diagnosis were recorded in 47 (3.2%). 
      These were found predominantly in young patients (median age 5 years), equally in 
      both sexes, and were seen to be associated with a low blood leucocyte count and 
      prolonged remissions.
