PMID- 6944596
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 19811118
LR  - 20071115
IS  - 0025-8458 (Print)
IS  - 0025-8458 (Linking)
VI  - 76
IP  - 19
DP  - 1981 Sep 11
TI  - [Can the course of an acute leukemia be predicted?].
PG  - 537-40
AB  - 65 unselected patients with acute leukemia, diagnosed in 1971 to 1978, were 
      analysed for prognostic factors. The survival-curves (constructed by means of 
      Kaplan-Meier-estimation) were compared with Logrank and generalized Wilcoxon 
      Test. Response to therapy, age, sex, initial granulocyte and platelet-count, LDH 
      and portion of peripheral blasts were examined. The median survival time of 
      patients with partial or complete remission (35.5 weeks) was almost six times as 
      long as in treated patients without remission. The prognosis got worse in higher 
      age. Women had with 7.5 weeks a shorter survival time compared to men with 23 
      weeks. The same was true for low initial platelet-count, high peripheral 
      blast-portion and high LDH. The morphologic type and initial granulocyte counts 
      had no prognostic value.
