DP  - 1980 May
TI  - Acute lymphoblastic leukemia.
PG  - 269-91
AB  - The improved outlook in childhood leukemia can be attributed to more accurate 
      diagnosis, better supportive care, the use of drug combinations to achieve and 
      maintain remission, and prophylactic therapy to prevent central nervous system 
      leukemia. With the best treatment available today, 65 to 70 per cent of children 
      are in complete continuous remission five years after diagnosis. Recent advances 
      in biology, diagnosis, and treatment which have contributed to this progress are 
      reviewed.
