VI  - 24
IP  - 4
DP  - 1980 Apr
TI  - Prognostic significance of amoeboid movement configuration in lymphoid cells from 
      children with acute lymphoblastic leukaemia.
PG  - 335-9
AB  - Bone marrow smears from 72 consecutive children with a recent diagnosis of acute 
      lymphoblastic leukaemia (ALL) have been morphologically analyzed. A high 
      incidence of lymphoid cells with amoeboid movement configuration (AMC) seems to 
      indicate a more favorable prognosis independently of other prognostic factors 
      e.g. age, WBC or sex. A positive correlation between the AMC and the mitotic 
      indices (MI) of the lymphoblasts indicates some connection between the motility 
      and the proliferative activity of the leukaemic cell clone.
