DP  - 1980
TI  - Acute lymphocytic leukemia masquerading as acute osteomyelitis. A report of two 
      cases.
PG  - 33-5
AB  - Two children each developed a focal destructive bone lesion accompanied by 
      intermittent fever, swelling, tenderness and elevated ESR. Blood counts were 
      normal; bone marrow aspiration showed acute leukemia. The bone lesions healed in 
      both patients after anti-leukemic therapy. We suggest that the similar 
      roentgenographic appearance of osteomyelitis, bone infarction and focal 
      destructive lesions in leukemia probably reflects a common, basically ischemic 
      process of bone.
