VI  - 2
IP  - 2
DP  - 1979
TI  - Prednimustine in adult acute myeloid leukaemia.
PG  - 133-6
AB  - In 23 patients with acute myeloid leukaemia (AML) and over the age of 64, four 
      remissions (17%) were obtained with Prednimustine as a single drug. The daily 
      dose was 24--60 mg orally. In 14 patients aged between 35 and 64 years who were 
      treated with Prednimustine 60--80 mg daily and vincristine 2.25 mg i.v. every 
      7--10 days, six remissions were obtained (43%). Upon remission, patients were 
      given ,0--40 mg of Prednimustine daily as maintenance therapy. Drug-induced 
      pancytopenia preceding remission was not recorded in any patient. There were no 
      side effects of major importance during maintenance therapy, and the median 
      duration of remission was 8 months. It is concluded that the low toxicity of 
      Prednimustine in normal bone marrow cells is of value, especially in elderly 
      patients with AML.
