DP  - 1979
TI  - Diagnostic value of leucocytic acid-phosphatase isoenzymes in determining 
      cytological types of non-lymphoid acute leukaemias.
PG  - 85-92
AB  - The normal isoenzymatic pattern of leucocytic acid-phosphatase based on the study 
      of 150 haematologically normal individuals is reported. The different pathologic 
      patterns of the leucocytic acid-phosphatase isoenzymes occurring in 
      non-lymphoblastic acute leukaemias are presented and correlated with the 
      subdivisions of acute leukaemias established by the French-American-British (FAB) 
      Co-operative Group. This study is considered to be especially useful in 
      identifying pure acute monocytic leukaemias corresponding to subtype M5 of the 
      FAB as well as acute erythraemias with unusual cytological and cytochemical 
      features.
