IP  - 1
DP  - 1978 Jan
TI  - A morphologic study of intracerebral hemorrhage in a case of acute leukemia.
PG  - 43-5
AB  - Morphologic studies have thus far failed to demonstrate the nature of the vessel 
      involved in the brain hemorrhages of patients with acute leukemia. A detailed 
      study of such hemorrhages was carried out in a patient with leukemic phase of 
      mycosis fungoides. Plastic-embedded lesions showed that blast cells blocked the 
      lumen of the capillary, leading to severe dilation and rupture of the vessel. The 
      rheologic properties of blast cells in vessels of critical diameters seem to be 
      an important factor in the pathogenesis of intracerebral hemorrhages.
