TI  - [Acute lymphoblastic leukemia an pericarditis (author's transl)].
PG  - 18-22
AB  - In a brief communication a case of acute lymphoblastic leukemia is presented, of 
      which the principal characteristics were: 1) An exceptional onset due to its 
      pleuropericardial manifestations while the hemogram was normal. 2) A quick 
      terminal evolution after a short and total remission. As far as authors know in 
      Spain, this localization has never been described primarily and in consulted 
      bibliography the appeared cases were always found in older patients. We call 
      attention to the pericardial effusions of a large volume in children in which the 
      diagnosis of classical pericarditis can't be quickly detected.
