VI  - 53
IP  - 1
DP  - 1975
TI  - Phagocytic activity of leukaemic blasts.
PG  - 17-24
AB  - Phagocytic activity of leukaemic blasts in 20 adults and 16 children suffering 
      from acute leukaemia was studied in vitro by the use of ferrioxidsaccharate. Most 
      frequently phagocytosing blasts were encountered in myelomonocytic leukaemias. 
      The morphological character of positive blasts resembled often that of monocytoid 
      cells. In lymphoblastic and reticular leukaemias phagocytic ability of blasts was 
      an exceptional finding.
