PMID- 4606364
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 19741220
LR  - 20190501
IS  - 0007-1447 (Print)
IS  - 0007-1447 (Linking)
VI  - 4
IP  - 5936
DP  - 1974 Oct 12
TI  - Combined T and B cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia.
PG  - 79-82
AB  - A case of acute lymphoblastic leukaemia in a 17-year-old male is described. The 
      patient had many distinctive features including a very high blast cell count, 
      prominent lymphadenopathy and hepatosplenomegaly, thymic mass, and a fulminant 
      clinical course. Immunological studies on the blast cells using a variety of 
      techniques showed the presence of two distinct subpopulations, one having the 
      surface characteristics of thymus-dependent (T) lymphoid cells and the other 
      those of bursa-equivalent (B) lymphoid cells. The case therefore represents the 
      first example of a combined T and B cell acute leukaemia.
